+# GPU Node Pools & NVMe Cache (example guidance)
+
+This document provides example commands and guidance for provisioning GPU node pools with local NVMe caching.
+
+GKE example (gcloud):
+1. Create GPU node pool:
+   gcloud container node-pools create gpu-pool \
+     --cluster=my-cluster --zone=us-central1-a \
+     --accelerator type=nvidia-tesla-a100,count=1 \
+     --machine-type=n1-standard-16 \
+     --num-nodes=2 \
+     --disk-type=local-ssd \
+     --local-ssd-count=1
+
+2. Label the pool nodes:
+   kubectl label nodes <node-name> node-role.kubernetes.io/gpu=true
+
+EKS / AKS: create equivalent nodegroups with GPU instance types and attach instance store or fast disks for caching.
+
+Recommendations:
+- Use nodeSelector in model-serving pods: nodeSelector: {"node-role.kubernetes.io/gpu":"true"}
+- Mount hostPath (/var/local/models) or use a CSI driver for node-local SSDs for model cache.
+- Deploy node-local cache DaemonSet (k8s/gpu/node-local-cache-daemonset.yaml) to prefetch candidate model shards.
